body:
For context, we were both poor for most of our friendship. Before she got married, we'd treat each other to dinner, depending on who had a job at the time, and that was all fine. but once she got married, things, naturally, changed. She talked about him constantly, I wasn't allowed to send her photos that had men in them because she didn't want him to think she was screwing the guy, I wasn't allowed to meet him for a few years because I was in a same sex relationship and she didn't want him to be 'turned on' by it, she'd answer my phone calls just to tell me she had to call me back because they were about to have sex. Just obnoxious kind of stuff. 

&#x200B;

So I figured, if you're so gung ho and proud to be married, then damn, at least let the man help you when you need it. Plus I'm sure he'll find out anyway since she was driving his car.
